Q: How to compare a u16 variable with a u16 enum A: <p>I suggest you parse the incoming value from the device as soon as possible and use that internally:</p>
<pre><code>enum ProtocolError {
  UnknownPacketType(u16),
}

impl TryFrom&lt;u16&gt; for Packets {
  type Error = ProtocolError;
  fn try_from(value: u16) -&gt; Result&lt;Self, Sefl::Error&gt; {
    match value {
      0xEF01 =&gt; Ok(Self::StartCode),
      0x01 =&gt; Ok(Self::CommandPacket),
      ...,
      _ =&gt; Err(ProtocolError::UknownPacketType(value))
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>you can then implement <code>Eq</code> for your <code>Packets</code> type and compare the incoming value</p>
<pre><code>#[derive(Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
#[repr(u16)]
pub enum Packets { ... }

let start: u16 = &lt;response from device&gt;
match Packets::try_from(start) {
  Ok(packet) =&gt; {
    if packet == Packets::StartCode {
      ...
    }
  },
  Err(e) =&gt; {
  // handle error
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>implementing <code>TryFrom</code> manually is pretty tedious so you can use a crate like <a href="https://docs.rs/strum/latest/strum/derive.FromRepr.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">FromRepr</a> to simplify it e.g.</p>
<pre><code>#[derive(Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, FromRepr)]
#[repr(u16)]
pub enum Packets { ... }
let start: u16 = &lt;response from device&gt;
match Packets::from_repr(start) {
}
</code></pre>

Q: Git pre-commit hook that automatically grants execution permissions (+x) on all .sh files which are being committed A: <p>This one liner uses <code>find</code> to identify files that don't have the execute bit set instead of looking for permission <code>644</code>, so it works with <em>unusual</em> patterns like <code>640</code> or even <code>200</code> (write only!):</p>
<pre><code>find . ! -perm -u+x -type f -name &quot;*.sh&quot; -exec git update-index --chmod=+x -- {} \;
</code></pre>
<p>Save it as the file <code>.git/hooks/pre-commit</code> (or <code>~/.githooks/pre-commit</code> for a global hook) and make it executable.</p>
<p>This longer version is what I use. It shows what it does and works on modified files only:</p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>#!/bin/bash

echo &quot;$(tput setaf 14)Fixing execute permission on scripts...$(tput sgr0)&quot;

for filename in $((git diff-index --cached --name-only HEAD; git diff-index --name-only HEAD) | sort -u)
do
    echo &quot;Making sure $filename is executable (if it needs to be)&quot;
    if [[ &quot;${filename}&quot; == *\.sh ]]
    then
        if [ -f &quot;${filename}&quot; ] &amp;&amp; [ ! -x &quot;${filename}&quot; ]
        then
            chmod -v +x &quot;$filename&quot;
            git update-index --chmod=+x -- &quot;$filename&quot;
        else
            echo &quot;$filename is already executable or a directory&quot;
        fi
    else
        echo &quot;$filename not a script&quot;
    fi
done
</code></pre>
